                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "This is one way to do it. Although needs `MiniPick.set_picker_target_window(vim.api.nvim_get_current_win())` call before `return true` for help window to be in focus after picking.\r\n\r\nIt also seems like a lot of code for what looks like a reasonable workflow. I am thinking about adding special option for default split direction.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">This is one way to do it. Although needs <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniPick.set_picker_target_window(vim.api.nvim_get_current_win())</code> call before <code class=\"notranslate\">return true</code> for help window to be in focus after picking.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It also seems like a lot of code for what looks like a reasonable workflow. I am thinking about adding special option for default split direction.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "This is one way to do it. Although needs MiniPick.set_picker_target_window(vim.api.nvim_get_current_win()) call before return true for help window to be in focus after picking.\nIt also seems like a lot of code for what looks like a reasonable workflow. I am thinking about adding special option for default split direction.",
